<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The high school SCP-2979 was first identified in is to be watched for further anomalous activity until 01/01/17</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a very awkward sentence. Later you state but then redact the name of the school:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230; was recovered from ██████ ███ High School.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I realize that you are usually not supposed to redact sections of the Containment Procedures in general, however, this skip would be better off having the name redacted in the Procedures than keeping the awkward wording you currently have.<br />
However, better than either of those is to just leave the name in the clear. And if you aren't comfortable using the name of a real school, just make one up or pick it at random:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Grand Ridge High School in Aethelney, MI is to be watched for further anomalous activity until 01/01/17.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>See, mutch better. And this is just something I pulled at random from <a href="http://fantasynamegenerators.com/school-names.php">http://fantasynamegenerators.com/school-names.php</a> and <a href="http://fantasynamegenerators.com/town_names.php">http://fantasynamegenerators.com/town_names.php</a>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This unanimously leads to a personality change within the host.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That is not what unanimously means.</p>
