<p>Well, again, the implication I'm trying (and failing, unfortunately) to make is that this name is one that- whatever it is- is impossible to accidentally come up with on your own. It may be made of sounds and letters completely foreign to human experience, something we literally are incapable of imagining because they are outside of our experience of what sound and language is.</p>
<p>Nobody can share the name,or accidentally come up with it, in the same way that no one can accidentally create a totally new color. Things like X-Rays can be seen by some animals, but not us, and we cannot even guess as to how it looks because it's so far outside of our experience. This name functions in a similar manner, in that it's so alien to us that we don't even have the capacity to accidentally come up with it by chance, no matter how many words or sounds we mix together.</p>
<p>In other words, it's not like Mr. Smith. It'd be closer to Mr. \°§!», only written with completely new symbols not present in any language.</p>

